      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Unto thee do I lift up mine eyes,\nO thou that sittest in the heavens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.123.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.123.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, as the eyes of servants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "look",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unto the hand of their master,\nAs the eyes of a maid unto the hand of her mistress;\nSo our eyes ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "look",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unto Jehovah our God,\nUntil he have mercy upon us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.123.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.123.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have mercy upon us, O Jehovah, have mercy upon us;\nFor we are exceedingly filled with contempt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.123.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.123.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our soul is exceedingly filled\nWith the scoffing of those that are at ease,\nAnd with the contempt of the proud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
